1. You may, free of charge:
   • download RemnaPilot from the official repository and run it on your own
     servers and on servers you administer, including for commercial purposes;
   • read the source code;
   • suggest fixes and ideas via Issues and Pull Requests in the official
     repository;
   • share a link to the official repository.

2. Without the author's written permission you may not:
   • distribute, publish or upload copies of RemnaPilot, in whole or in part,
     modified or not — on websites, channels, chats, archives or repositories
     outside GitHub;
   • sell, rent or include RemnaPilot in paid products, bundles, server images
     or services;
   • present RemnaPilot or its parts as your own work, or remove or change this
     notice, the author's name or links to the official repository.

3. Forking on GitHub is allowed to the extent provided by the GitHub Terms of
   Service — for viewing and preparing Pull Requests. This does not grant the
   right to distribute the fork as a separate product.

4. THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND. The author is
   not liable for any damage arising from its use. Back up before making changes
   on production servers.

5. RemnaPilot versions before 2.1 were published under the MIT license. These
   terms apply to version 2.1 and all later versions.

To request permission: open an Issue in the official repository.
